sdata> -- BREAK's debug sub-prompt (Inspect_PDV) shares the same missing-echo
sdata> -- defect as Run_REPL's top-level prompt (ADR-061, pe7_statement_echo.cmd),
sdata> -- reachable under piped/non-tty stdin exactly like Run_REPL's own case --
sdata> -- Interactive_Mode is True for the whole REPL session regardless of tty
sdata> -- status, so the debug prompt loop runs and reads real commands (CONTINUE
sdata> -- here) via the same unechoed Get_Line pattern ADR-061 fixes at the top
sdata> -- level. Direct regression guard, written to Standard_Error to match this
sdata> -- prompt's own stream.
sdata> NEW
sdata> REPEAT 2
sdata> LET X = RECNO()
sdata> BREAK
sdata> RUN
[debug:record 1]> CONTINUE
[debug:record 2]> CONTINUE
RUN complete. 2 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> QUIT
